  "subject": "A day-shift hotel receptionist in Taichung has quietly kept room 307 for a regular Tuesday salesman for a year, writes his name in the register, and finally decides to give him hers.",
  "caption": "1970s Taiwanese hotel-lounge shuffle, laid-back swung groove. Hammond B3 organ with slow Leslie swirl and soft chord stabs, walking upright bass, brushed snare and ride, clean nylon-string guitar comping offbeats. Warm vintage tape saturation, dry intimate lounge room. Female vocal, warm mid register, relaxed, clearly sung melody. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 104 BPM, G major. Bashful, gently swinging mood. No synthesizers, no autotune, no trap drums, no distorted guitar, no rap.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n拜二下晡五點半\n皮箱輾過大理石\n三〇七號免問伊\n我的筆已經寫好勢\n[Pre-Chorus]\n伊笑一下講「我來矣」\n我的心就綴咧跳\n[Chorus]\n三〇七號房，毋是我的房\n住的是伊，等的是我\n登記簿頂寫伊的名\n我偷偷寫一个「咱」\n[Verse]\n伊愛的茶是燒烏龍\n毋免問，我先泡好勢\n伊問我，敢猶袂下班\n我講猶有一點鐘\n[Pre-Chorus]\n伊接過房卡講多謝\n我的手煞囥袂好\n[Chorus]\n三〇七號房，毋是我的房\n伊來的日，我上有精神\n登記簿頂寫伊的名\n我偷偷寫一个「咱」\n[Verse]\n這禮拜伊的電話無來\n我共三〇七留到十點\n經理問我欲賣予別人\n我講彼間，已經有人\n[Bridge]\n大門拍開，拖皮箱的聲\n我聽一擺就知是伊\n[Chorus]\n三〇七號房，毋是我的房\n今仔日我欲開喙講\n登記簿頂寫伊的名\n這擺，換我寫我的\n[Outro]\n暗安，三〇七，歡迎轉來\n這擺，我先共伊講我的名",
